Copyright 2026 AIterprise

This product includes data derived from third-party sources, each under its own terms:

- OSV records, obtained through https://osv.dev and trimmed to the fields the scanner reads
  (most text is removed). Each record keeps the licence of the database it came from, and its
  id prefix names that database:
  - data/ait/malicious-versions.json.gz: MAL- records from OpenSSF Malicious Packages,
    https://github.com/ossf/malicious-packages, Apache-2.0.
  - data/ait/vuln-subset.json.gz: GHSA- records from the GitHub Advisory Database,
    https://github.com/github/advisory-database, CC-BY 4.0; and PYSEC- records from the
    PyPI Advisory Database, https://github.com/pypa/advisory-database, CC-BY 4.0.
  The builders keep only records from these databases (tools/osv_terms.py) and write the list,
  with a record count for each, into the file's "terms" field; records from any other database
  are left out. A unit test checks every record id shipped in both files.
- CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog (data/ait/kev.json) — public domain (CC0).
- Known-bad model-file hashes (data/ait/known-bad-hashes.json) — SHA-256 and SHA-1 values of
  malicious files as published in incident reports by Rapid7, ReversingLabs and Pluto Security.
  Each entry links the report it was copied from; the descriptions are AIterprise's own words.
- Model and dataset licence verdicts (data/ait/licence-verdicts.json) are AIterprise
  summaries of the cited licence texts. They are advisory and are not legal advice.

First-party AIterprise data, Apache-2.0 like the code: data/ait/taxonomy.json,
data/ait/ai-assets.json (prompt file names, AI provider API hosts, vector-store images and calls),
data/ait/command-rules.json, data/ait/poison-patterns.json, data/ait/model-rules.json,
data/ait/popular-packages.json (package names only) and data/ait/rule-quality.json
(false-positive measurements, see tools/measure_fp.py).

No third-party source code is vendored in this repository. Ed25519 (RFC 8032) and the minisign
format are implemented from their specifications.
